IPv4 utilities (parse, subnet, range-expand, to-ipv6)

Usage: ubertool ipv4 [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  parse         Parse an IPv4 address and emit its representations
  subnet        Compute subnet info for a CIDR block
  range-expand  Expand a CIDR block into a list of addresses (capped by --max)
  to-ipv6       Convert IPv4 to IPv4-mapped IPv6 form (::ffff:a.b.c.d)
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json     Output as JSON to stdout. Human messages still go to stderr
  -q, --quiet    Bare values only (pipe-friendly)
  -v, --verbose  Verbose progress to stderr
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
